```

Much more complex, but scales to books, repositories, websites, and large knowledge bases.

---

If your goal is to become a strong AI engineer, I would learn chunking in this order:

1. Fixed-size chunking
2. RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter
3. Markdown/Header chunking
4. Token-based chunking
5. Semantic chunking
6. Parent-child retrieval
7. Contextual retrieval
8. Hybrid search (BM25 + Vector)
9. Rerankers
10. Agentic RAG

The biggest quality jump in real-world RAG systems usually comes not from fancy chunking, but from **hybrid search + reranking + good metadata**. Many teams spend weeks tuning chunk sizes and get less improvement than adding a reranker.
